**assistant**:
> Yes. Its useful ideas are **only partially represented**:
> 
> - `PlanSelector` learns plan-level satisfaction/risk/cost/latency.
> - `ModelRouter` has per-model success/failure evidence, but it is currently **in-memory, never updated, non-exploratory, and lacks observed latency/usage learning**.
> - Feedback is attributed to the selected plan, but not to the resolved outer model (or nested JS `llm.*` model calls).
> 
> I would **not restore `BayesSelector` as a parallel selector**. Incorporate its useful behavior into `ModelRouter` and persistence.
> 
> ## Recommended design
> 
> 1. **Persist model-invocation evidence**, keyed at least by:
>    ```text
>    (model_id, version, purpose, capability/task bucket)
>    ```
>    Store successes, failures, invocation count, observed latency distribution, token counts, and observed cost.
> 
> 2. Add a `ModelCallTrace` / `ModelInvocationRecord` rather than forcing this into aggregate `ResponseMetrics`. A response may make multiple calls: initial answer, synthesis, and `llm.text` calls inside JavaScript.
> 
> 3. Change `ModelRouter.resolve()` from deterministic `max(score)` to bounded exploration—ideally Thompson sampling:
>    \[
>    q_m \sim \operatorname{Beta}(\alpha_m,\beta_m)
>    \]
>    \[
>    U_m = w_q q_m - w_c \widehat C_m - w_l \widehat L_m
>    \]
>    Choose stochastically among eligible models, with exploration disabled or tightly constrained for high-risk tasks.
> 
> 4. On provider completion, record **objective execution evidence**:
>    - success/failure;
>    - observed latency;
>    - provider token usage and cost where available;
>    - timeout/rate-limit/provider-error class.
> 
> 5. On `vote_up/down`, also update the outer resolved model’s satisfaction evidence—but keep this separate from provider reliability. Do **not** blindly credit every nested model call equally; use explicit attribution weights or reserve user feedback for the final synthesis model.
> 
> 6. Permit fallback/retry only before visible output. Record each attempted model invocation and failure. After visible output starts, never switch models.
> 
> ## Important corrections to the old implementation
> 
> - Its denominator should be Beta-style `successes + failures + 2`, not `+ len(responders)`.
> - Avoid mutable `last_responder`; `ResponseRecord.model_id/version` is the durable attribution key.
> - Replace its arbitrary “$1/minute” conversion with explicit independently configurable cost and latency weights.
> - Measure output tokens too; prompt-token throughput alone is misleading.
> - Do not treat provider failures, thumbs-down, and quality failures as one signal.
> 
> In short: retain BayesSelector’s **exploration under uncertainty plus empirical cost/latency/reliability**, but implement it as persisted, trace-based evidence in `ModelRouter`, while `PlanSelector` remains responsible for choosing the top-level execution mode.
